{"command": "cd /testbed && sed -n '113,130p' specs/001-transactions/spec.md; echo ===; grep -c \"NEEDS CLARIFICATION\" specs/001-transactions/spec.md; echo ===; cat specs/001-transactions/checklists/requirements.md | head -30", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "## Requirements *(mandatory)*\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n- **FR-001**: The system MUST provide a batch writer that wraps a supplied TinyDB database instance and operates on the default table only, without changing the database's ordinary public behavior.\n- **FR-002**: The batch writer MUST expose an `apply` capability that accepts a list of operation dictionaries, where each operation is either `{'op':'insert','document':<document>}` or `{'op':'remove','doc_id':<positive integer>}`. A non-list input MUST be rejected with `ValueError`.\n- **FR-003**: `apply` MUST validate and apply the operations sequentially and MUST return a list containing only the IDs of inserted documents, in submission order; removes MUST add no result; empty input MUST return `[]`.\n- **FR-004**: `apply` MUST raise `ValueError` for unknown or malformed operations (non-dict entry, unknown `op`, missing `document`/`doc_id`, non-positive-integer `doc_id`, non-dict `document`). `bool` values MUST be rejected as `doc_id` even though they are integer subclasses. Operations MUST be validated structurally before any change is committed: unsupported fields (fields beyond `op`/`document`/`doc_id`, or `document` on a remove / `doc_id` on an insert), non-list operation inputs, and non-dict documents MUST each raise `ValueError`. An empty dictionary MUST be accepted as a document.\n- **FR-004a**: The batch writer MUST expose a `preview` capability that returns the list of inserted document IDs that `apply` of the same operations would produce, without changing any table data, without consuming or advancing the next insertion ID, and without affecting existing table handles or query caches; on any error it MUST raise `ValueError` with zero side effects. Each `preview` call MUST return a new, detached list: mutating a previously returned preview list MUST NOT affect subsequent preview results or any internal state.\n- **FR-004b**: A successful `apply` MUST advance the wrapper's next-insertion-ID state by the number of documents inserted in the batch and MUST persist that state to the underlying table so that subsequent inserts - via `apply` or via ordinary `db.insert` - continue the ID sequence without reuse or rewind, even across remove operations. A failed `apply` MUST NOT consume any IDs.\n- **FR-004c**: The batch writer MUST observe the database's current state on every call: ordinary `db.insert` operations performed between calls MUST be seen by the wrapper, and no stale initial snapshot MAY be cached.\n- **FR-005**: Batch application MUST be atomic: on any error during the batch, the complete pre-batch default-table data MUST be restored, including undoing inserts applied earlier in the same batch.\n- **FR-006**: A `remove` targeting a document ID that does not exist in the default table MUST be treated as an error and MUST trigger rollback.\n- **FR-007**: Handles to the default table acquired before a batch MUST reflect both successful application and rollback.\n- **FR-008**: Ordinary TinyDB reads and writes, and pre-existing documents, MUST continue to work unchanged while the batch writer is in use.\n- **FR-009**: Inserted data and returned data MUST NOT alias the caller's input; mutating an operation after `apply` MUST NOT mutate the database, and mutating returned or stored nested data MUST NOT affect the caller's input or the database.\n\n### Key Entities *(include if feature involves data)*\n===\n0\n===\n# Specification Quality Checklist: Atomic Batch Transactions for TinyDB\n\n**Purpose**: Validate specification completeness and quality before proceeding to planning\n**Created**: 2026-10-17\n**Feature**: [spec.md](../spec.md)\n\n## Content Quality\n\n- [x] No implementation details 